  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(7\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 10 = 70\n\\]\n\nSince \\(70 \\le 100\\), she has enough shrimp available. Therefore, Emily can peel and sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]\n\nshrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nSince she has 100 shrimp available, she can peel and sauté \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp in ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nShe discards \\(5\\) damaged shrimp afterward, leaving:\n\n\\[\n60 - 5 = 55\n\\]\n\nSo, Emily can peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp, of which \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain after discarding the damaged ones.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s peeling rate is unchanged:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nSo she can peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp in ten minutes. After discarding \\(5\\), \\(55\\) shrimp remain.\n\nHer sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nIn ten minutes, she can sauté:\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, she can peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp, but she can sauté only \\(\\boxed{25}\\) of them in ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60 - 5 = 55\n\\]\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in ten minutes. Therefore, in ten minutes, she can peel \\(60\\) shrimp and sauté \\(\\boxed{30}\\) shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Because Emily works sequentially, add the peeling and sautéing times.\n\n- Peeling rate: \\(6\\) shrimp/minute, so each takes \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute.\n- Sautéing rate: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes \\(=3\\) shrimp/minute, so each takes \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute.\n\nIf \\(x\\) shrimp are successfully sautéed, Emily must peel \\(x+5\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are discarded. Thus:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x+5}{6}+\\frac{x}{3}\\le 10\n\\]\n\nMultiplying by \\(6\\):\n\n\\[\nx+5+2x\\le 60\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3x\\le 55\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx\\le 18.33\n\\]\n\nTherefore, she can successfully sauté \\(\\boxed{18}\\) shrimp. She peels \\(18+5=\\boxed{23}\\) shrimp total, with \\(5\\) discarded.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily sautés \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes, so her sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{10}=3\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nTo cook \\(90\\) shrimp, she must peel \\(90+5=95\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are discarded.\n\nPeeling time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{95}{6}=15\\tfrac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSautéing time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{3}=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSince she works sequentially:\n\n\\[\n15\\tfrac{5}{6}+30=45\\tfrac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, it will take Emily \\(\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
